:"owid-transport","note":"One passenger, ~3,980 km at ~151 g CO2e/km including non-CO2 warming."},{"id":"train-km","symbol":"tram.fill","singular":"km by train","plural":"km by train","gramsPerUnit":35.0,"citationId":"owid-transport","note":"Per passenger, UK national rail average."},{"id":"shower","symbol":"shower.fill","singular":"hot shower","plural":"hot showers","gramsPerUnit":857.9,"citationId":"epa-watersense","note":"10 minutes at 2.0 gpm, water heated by 25 °C electrically (~2.3 kWh), on your selected grid."},{"id":"macbook","symbol":"laptopcomputer","singular":"MacBook charge","plural":"MacBook charges","gramsPerUnit":22.38,"citationId":"apple-mba","note":"52.6 Wh battery, ~60 Wh from the wall, on your selected grid."},{"id":"led-year","symbol":"lightbulb.fill","singular":"year of an LED bulb left on","plural":"years of an LED bulb left on","gramsPerUnit":32697.18,"citationId":"doe-led","note":"A 10 W LED burning day and night for a year (~88 kWh), on your selected grid."},{"id":"gasoline","symbol":"fuelpump.fill","singular":"gallon of gasoline","plural":"gallons of gasoline","gramsPerUnit":8887.0,"citationId":"epa-vehicle","note":"CO2 from burning one US gallon."},{"id":"burger","symbol":"fork.knife","singular":"quarter-pound beef burger","plural":"quarter-pound beef burgers","gramsPerUnit":11283.3,"citationId":"owid-food","note":"113 g of beef-herd beef at ~99.5 kg CO2e/kg."},{"id":"us-day","symbol":"person.fill","singular":"day of an average American's emissions","plural":"days of an average American's emissions","gramsPerUnit":39151.266255989045,"citationId":"owid-co2","note":"~14.3 t fossil CO2 per person per year."},{"id":"tree","symbol":"tree.fill","singular":"tree-decade of absorption","plural":"tree-decades of absorption","gramsPerUnit":60000.0,"citationId":"epa-equivalencies","note":"CO2 one urban tree seedling takes up over 10 years."},{"id":"gemini-prompt","symbol":"sparkles","singular":"median Gemini prompt","plural":"median Gemini prompts","gramsPerUnit":0.03,"citationId":"google-2025","note":"Google's measured median text prompt, May 2025. A short chat prompt, not an agentic coding turn."}],"citations":[{"id":"epoch-2025","title":"How much energy does ChatGPT use?","publisher":"Epoch AI","year":2025,"url":"https://epoch.ai/gradient-updates/how-much-energy-does-chatgpt-use","usedFor":"~0.3 Wh for a typical GPT-4o reply (~500 output tokens) on H100s, an upper-leaning estimate. One anchor for the 2024 baseline."},{"id":"jegham-2025","title":"How Hungry is AI? Benchmarking Energy, Water, and Carbon Footprint of LLM Inference","publisher":"Jegham et al., arXiv:2505.09598","year":2025,"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.09598","usedFor":"~0.42 Wh for a short GPT-4o query (incl. data-centre overhead), and a 65x+ spread between the most and least efficient models. Second anchor for the baseline and the tier spread."},{"id":"google-2025","title":"Measuring the environmental impact of delivering AI at Google scale","publisher":"Google, arXiv:2508.15734","year":2025,"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2508.15734","usedFor":"Median Gemini text prompt = 0.24 Wh / 0.03 gCO2e. Energy per prompt fell 33x in 12 months. Accelerator-only accounting gives 0.10 Wh, so idle capacity and host overhead must be counted."},{"id":"chung-2026","title":"Where Do the Joules Go? Diagnosing Inference Energy Consumption","publisher":"Chung et al. (ML.ENERGY), arXiv:2601.22076","year":2026,"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2601.22076","usedFor":"Measured H100 and B200 energy per token across 46 models. Reasoning workloads cost ~2.1x more per token, because long sequences limit batch size."},{"id":"mlenergy-2025","title":"The ML.ENERGY Benchmark: Toward Automated Inference Energy Measurement and Optimization","publisher":"Chung et al., arXiv:2505.06371","year":2025,"url":"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.06371","usedFor":"Open, measured per-token inference energy for open-weight models. Basis for the prefill-versus-decode and size scaling."},{"id":"mistral-2025","title":"Our contribution to a global environmental standard for AI","publisher":"Mistral AI","year":2025,"url":"https://mistral.ai/news/our-contribution-to-a-global-environmental-standard-for-ai","usedFor":"Full life-cycle figure of 1.14 gCO2e per 400-token Le Chat reply (incl. hardware manufacturing). A cross-check that our per-reply grams are in the right range."},{"id":"egrid-2022","title":"eGRID2022 Summary Data (US total output emission rate)","publisher":"US EPA","year":2024,"url":"https://www.epa.gov/egrid/summary-data","usedFor":"US average grid intensity of ~823 lb CO2/MWh (~373 g/kWh). Default location-based grid factor."},{"id":"ember-2025","title":"Global Electricity Review 2025","publisher":"Ember","year":2025,"url":"https://ember-energy.org/latest-insights/global-electricity-review-2025/","usedFor":"World average grid intensity of ~473 gCO2/kWh in 2024."},{"id":"google-pue","title":"Power usage effectiveness","publisher":"Google Data Centers","year":2024,"url":"https://datacenters.google/efficiency/","usedFor":"Hyperscale fleet PUE of ~1.09–1.10. Industry surveys report ~1.5 for typical facilities. Default PUE 1.15 sits between them, leaning hyperscale."},{"id":"epa-vehicle","title":"Greenhouse Gas Emissions from a Typical Passenger Vehicle","publisher":"US EPA","year":2023,"url":"https://www.epa.gov/greenvehicles/greenhouse-gas-emissions-typical-passenger-vehicle","usedFor":"~400 g CO2 per mile for an average passenger car, and 8,887 g CO2 per gallon of gasoline."},{"id":"epa-equivalencies","title":"Greenhouse Gas Equivalencies Calculator: Calculations and References","publisher":"US EPA","year":2024,"url":"https://www.epa.gov/energy/greenhouse-gas-equivalencies-calculator-calculations-and-references","usedFor":"~60 kg CO2 taken up by one urban tree seedling grown for 10 years."},{"id":"iea-streaming","title":"The carbon footprint of streaming video: fact-checking the headlines","publisher":"IEA (G. Kamiya)","year":2020,"url":"https://www.iea.org/commentaries/the-carbon-footprint-of-streaming-video-fact-checking-the-headlines","usedFor":"~36 g CO2 per hour of streamed video (2019 global average)."},{"id":"owid-transport","title":"Which form of transport has the smallest carbon footprint?","publisher":"Our World in Data (from UK BEIS factors)","year":2023,"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/travel-carbon-footprint","usedFor":"~151 g CO2e per passenger-km for a short-haul flight, including non-CO2 warming."},{"id":"owid-food","title":"Environmental Impacts of Food Production (Poore & Nemecek 2018 data)","publisher":"Our World in Data","year":2021,"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/environmental-impacts-of-food","usedFor":"~99.5 kg CO2e per kg of beef from beef herds (global mean incl. supply-chain losses)."},{"id":"owid-co2","title":"CO2 emissions per capita","publisher":"Our World in Data / Global Carbon Project","year":2024,"url":"https://ourworldindata.org/co2-emissions","usedFor":"US fossil CO2 of ~14.3 t per person per year."},{"id":"nhts-2017","title":"Summary of Travel Trends: 2017 National Household Travel Survey","publisher":"US FHWA","year":2018,"url":"https://nhts.ornl.gov/assets/2017_nhts_summary_travel_trends.pdf","usedFor":"Average US commute trip of ~11.7 miles one way. Default commute length."},{"id":"eia-home","title":"How much electricity does an American home use?","publisher":"US EIA","year":2023,"url":"https://www.eia.gov/tools/faqs/faq.php?id=97&t=3","usedFor":"Average US home uses ~10,791 kWh of electricity per year (2022), about 29.6 kWh a day."},{"id":"epa-watersense","title":"WaterSense Labeled Showerheads","publisher":"US EPA","year":2024,"url":"https://www.epa.gov/watersense/showerheads","usedFor":"Standard showerhead flow of 2.5 gpm (WaterSense: ≤2.0). A 10-minute shower at 2.0 gpm heated by 25 °C needs ~2.2 kWh of heat, ~2.3 kWh from an electric heater."},{"id":"apple-mba","title":"MacBook Air 13-inch Technical Specifications","publisher":"Apple","year":2024,"url":"https://www.ap